From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: a733: the display-engine node and the TCON-to-DisplayPort edge

Two things the pixel path's device tree has been missing, and one comment that
is no longer true.

THE PIPELINE NODE. `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-de-to-tcon-edge` added the display engine and the DE -> TCON_TV1 edge
and deliberately left out the node that names the pipeline as a whole, saying
in its own header that "the patch that settles the driver shape adds it". `drm-a733-kms-drm-device-for-the-display-pipe`
settles it, so it is here:

    display-engine {
            compatible = "allwinner,sun60i-a733-display-engine";
            allwinner,pipelines = <&mixer0>;
    };

It carries no reg, no clock and no interrupt because it is not a block -- it is
the list of pipelines a KMS driver has to bring up together, which is why it
sits at the root beside `soc` rather than inside it. `allwinner,pipelines` is
mainline sun4i-drm's own property (sun4i_drv.c walks it to build its component
match list), reused verbatim rather than invented, on the same bet `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-de-to-tcon-edge` made
when it claimed mainline's DE33 mixer compatible: write the device tree in the
shape the driver we intend to converge on already expects, so converging is a
code change and not a device-tree change.

ONE ENTRY, and `drm-a733-kms-drm-device-for-the-display-pipe` refuses more. This SoC's display engine has two display
outputs and could drive a second pipe, but only
disp0 -> TCON_TV1 -> DisplayPort has ever been on a board.

THE TCON -> TRANSMITTER EDGE. tcon_tv1 gains ports/port@1 and edp0 gains
ports/port@0. This is what of_drm_find_bridge() resolves: `drm-a733-kms-drm-device-for-the-display-pipe` asks
devm_drm_of_get_bridge() for port 1 endpoint 0 of the TCON node, follows the
graph to the transmitter, and finds the drm_bridge `drm-a733-dp-register-a-drm-bridge` published with
drm_bridge_add(). Port 1 is the output side by the same convention port@0 uses
for the input, and the numbers are read by the driver, not by a binding.

⚠ THE COMMENT THAT WAS TRUE AND IS NOT. `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-de-to-tcon-edge`'s mixer0 node carried a paragraph
saying this edge was "deliberately NOT here" because the DP's shape -- bridge
or encoder component -- was undecided, and recording the debt. It is decided
and the debt is paid, so the paragraph is deleted rather than struck through,
per this tree's rule that a file holds only what is true now.

WHAT THIS DOES NOT ADD, named so it is not read as an oversight
----------------------------------------------------------------

⬜ THE CONNECTOR IS STILL NOT DESCRIBED. The Type-C receptacle's `displayport`
property -- what would let dp_altmode_probe() find the transmitter node's
connector for out-of-band hot-plug -- exists in displayport.c:800-804 and in NO
binding: usb-connector.yaml is `unevaluatedProperties: false` and documents
only an `altmodes/displayport` CHILD NODE, which does not satisfy that lookup.
`drm-a733-dp-register-a-drm-bridge` records the same debt from the driver side. It is closed by one
observation once a connector exists -- plug the monitor and read
/sys/class/drm/<card>-DP-1/status -- and not by adding a property no schema
accepts.

⬜ NO BINDING SCHEMA. No display node in this tree has one -- not the mixer,
not the TCON, not the transmitter -- so a schema for the pipeline node alone
would describe the least of it. The debt is the display track's, not this
patch's.

That is the same exception `clk-sunxi-ng-a733-add-edp-bus-gate-and-reset` to `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-de-to-tcon-edge` already carry and each states in its
own header. Highest misc number in the applied tree is `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-de-to-tcon-edge` (`clk-sunxi-ng-a733-display-engine-clock-gate-reset` and `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-de-to-tcon-edge` are in
flight on display/engine-ccu-dt); next free is `arm64-dts-a733-display-engine-node-and-tcon-dp-edge`, which is this one.

WHAT IS VERIFIED
-----------------

✅ Applies at --fuzz=0 and the dtb compiles (`compile-check` builds
sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s-minimal.dtb).

⬜ NOTHING HERE HAS BEEN ON A BOARD. A device-tree node that nothing binds
changes no register, and until `drm-a733-kms-drm-device-for-the-display-pipe` binds it this one changes nothing at all.
The observable it serves is `drm-a733-kms-drm-device-for-the-display-pipe`'s: /dev/fb0 at 1920x1200.

Assisted-by: Claude

